// The VS Code extension: its language client, the languages it
// contributes, the live preview, the commands it runs, how it's packaged,
// and the errors it shows.
include = [
  "./client.heron.md",
  "./languages.heron.md",
  "./preview.heron.md",
  "./commands.heron.md",
  "./package.heron.md",
  "./fixing.heron.md",
  "./errors.heron",
]

| [The editor extension](#system.editor_extension) brings Heron to VS Code and the editors built on it,
| such as Cursor and VSCodium. It's a client of [the language server](#system.language_server):
| everything it knows about a tree comes from `heron lsp`, so the editor never disagrees with
| `heron check` and `heron lint`. It ships as one `.vsix` file.
